# @edc/web — every environment variable this app reads.
#
# Copy to `.env` for local development. All of these are SERVER-side: they are
# read through `$env/dynamic/private` (or `process.env` in the Vite config) and
# never reach the browser. There is no PUBLIC_* var — the browser only ever
# talks to this app's own `/api/**` proxy routes.

# ── Backends ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Payload/Next backend (identity + sessions, messages, documents, ratings,
# publication). Docker: use the compose service name. Deployed: the app's
# https host.
#
# ⚠ Renamed from CHAT_BACKEND_URL, to match the backend's own move to
# PUBLIC_BACKEND_URL / EDC_ENV. Infra config must follow.
BACKEND_URL=http://localhost:3002

# ai-service base URL. REQUIRED — there is no fallback on purpose: this app
# listens on :3000 itself, so a localhost default would loop it back to itself.
AI_SERVICE_URL=http://localhost:3001

# ai-service app-role bearer. REQUIRED. Server-only — never in the client
# bundle. Rotate by changing it here; no code change needed.
AI_SERVICE_API_KEY=replace-me

# ── Tenancy ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The ai-service tenant key a turn is billed and scoped to. One value per
# deployment, NOT per user — nothing in the session proves a user's ai-service
# tenant. Defaults to `edc` when unset.
ORG_KEY=edc

# ── Prompt source ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Where the generation spec comes from: unset/anything = this app's inline
# override (today's behaviour); `registry` = let ai-service's prompt registry
# supply it. Only set `registry` AFTER the backend has seeded the registry row,
# or every turn 400s. Rollback is unsetting it — no deploy.
# ⚠ Renamed from CHAT_PROMPT_SOURCE. Only this app reads it.
# PROMPT_SOURCE=registry

# Query expansion: before searching, the cheap model rewords the question
# (2 rewordings + 1 hypothetical answer), all are searched and fused by RRF.
# One extra `quick` model call per turn. Default ON; `off` turns it off.
# QUERY_EXPANSION=off

# Cross-encoder rerank on each corpus retrieve (ai-service `rerank: true`).
# Default ON; `off` retrieves without it. A failing rerank falls back to the
# plain retrieve. See src/lib/server/engine/rerank.ts.
# CHAT_RERANK=off

# (CHAT_RETRIEVE_ASSISTANT_CHUNKS is gone, 2026-10-21: conversation turns are
# always dropped from the chat SOURCES, with no switch. See
# src/lib/server/engine/chunkFence.ts and src/lib/turnChunks.ts.)

# Earlier conversations as ORIENTATION, never cited (owner ruling 2026-10-21,
# #4 choice A). One extra retrieve per turn over the ecosistema's corpus
# (top 3 turns, 1,500 chars), shown to the model as "Conversaciones
# anteriores (no son fuentes; no las cites)". The current conversation is
# always excluded. `ecosistema` (default): every member's anonymised turns;
# `own`: only this user's other conversations; `off`: no leg. Unknown is
# `off`. Read per turn. See src/lib/server/engine/orientation.ts.
# CHAT_ORIENT_SCOPE=ecosistema

# Chat retrieval mode: `dense` (default) or `hybrid` (one /v1/retrieve/multi
# call, cosine + Spanish keyword search; needs ai-service `metadataFilterIn`).
# See src/lib/server/engine/hybrid.ts and infra/.env.example.
# CHAT_RETRIEVAL_MODE=hybrid

# Chat prompt cite rule. Unset means `E` (the default since 2026-10-22): always
# answer, documents first with [N], then general knowledge in a part opening
# "Fuera de los documentos:", which lists no source; off-topic questions get an
# answer with 0 sources; E also changes the source rule in
# src/lib/server/citationProvenance.ts. Still selectable for comparison: `A`
# (the 8a1df66 rule), `B` (cite less, answer more), `C` (B's citation limit, no
# no-answer instruction), `D` (B plus a partial-answer example). Case and spaces
# are ignored; an unknown value logs a warning and runs `E`. Read per request
# from the runtime env, so a change needs only a container recreate, no
# rebuild. The first turn (and any change) logs `[prompt] cite variant X` at
# info level; every turn logs it at debug level. Texts: CITE_RULE_VARIANTS in
# src/lib/server/engine/prompt.ts.
# CHAT_CITE_VARIANT=A

# An answer with no [N] lists the top 3 retrieved passages, but only those the
# cross-encoder scored at or above this floor. Chunks with no rerank score
# (rerank off or failed) are always kept. 0 turns the floor off. Default 0.1,
# inferred from a small Spark sample (relevant 0.99-1.0, irrelevant <=1e-4).
# Each fallback logs `[sources] fallback rerank floor=... top=[...]` at info.
# CHAT_FALLBACK_MIN_RERANK=0.1

# /grafo full-text search box (backlog #31).
GRAPH_SEARCH_ENABLED=true

# ── Runtime / dev server ───────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Port. Read by vite.config.ts in dev (default 5173) and by adapter-node in
# production (the image sets 3000).
# PORT=5173

# Bind address for the production Node server. The image sets 0.0.0.0.
# HOST=0.0.0.0

# Set to `true` to make Vite poll for file changes instead of using inotify.
# Needed only for HMR across a bind mount inside the dev container.
# CHOKIDAR_USEPOLLING=true
